  m_OnCullStateChanged:
    m_PersistentCalls:
      m_Calls: []
  m_text: '<b>PRINCIPLE:</b>

    When metal salts are introduced into the non-luminous
    flame of a Bunsen burner, thermally excited valence electrons absorb energy and
    jump to higher energy levels. Upon returning to their ground state, they emit
    light of characteristic wavelengths/frequencies within the visible spectrum.



    Volatile
    chlorides are formed by mixing the salt with Conc. HCl:

    Salt + Conc. HCl 
    ==>  Metal Chloride Paste'
